7
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,860
So what is Armageddon?

8
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:42,580
Armageddon is a brand new mode eliminator.

9
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:50,350
It combines highly efficient enzymes, kinases, glucanases, and lysosomes with geranium, enhanced by AI and fusion protein technology.

10
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:51,890
What did we achieve?

11
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:58,830
Initially, we successfully expressed most wild-type enzymes except PR-CHA, which forms inclusion bodies.

12
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:09,620
Performance testing then showed that gel-nax HIV was inactive and BGLS2-7 has low activity. Thus, these three underperforming enzymes were selected for AI optimization.

13
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:18,290
As a side note, human life exam and alpha-cluconase, AGLE K14 did not achieve expression and requirements for the investigation.

14
00:01:19,050 --> 00:01:27,440
To optimize in-time performance, we interviewed with expert Mr. Hsu, who inspired us to use deep learning based modeling tools, protein MPN and ligand MPN.

15
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:37,650
Following this idea, we developed a protein engineering pipeline that includes sequence redesign by the two NPN models after selecting redesign residues by MSA.

16
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:44,460
After the redesign, we evaluated the generated variance using AlphaFold, Rosetta, and Glide.

17
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:51,440
Glide is used for ligand docking and is selected after comparing several docking engines for docking of large carbohydrates.

18
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:56,780
A custom docking method was then developed, which combines glide docking with structural alignment.

19
00:01:57,510 --> 00:02:01,900
After evaluation, the best performing variants are set as candidates for wet lab.

